{"timestamp":"2026-09-05T04:58:41.445Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06fee-e1a4-7961-b70d-efecc1d6f35b","call_id":"call_mXcruyROat2d0RGIG06tqWc2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\"\"\"P4Flat KV cache compressor.\n\nDrop-in ``kv_compressor`` for ``DualMemoryLoader`` that uses the BF16 P4-flat\ncodec (per-64x64-tile 16-entry exponent palette + 4-bit code + raw\nsign|mantissa byte, with out-of-palette exponents kept as an exception list).\nSelected with ``--kv-comp p4flat`` (``TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_BACKEND=p4flat``).\n\nLike :class:`DietGPUKVCompressor` the base :class:`P4FlatKVCompressor` is a\nGPU-kernel backend (no C++ worker threads): ``compress_batch_async`` launches\nthe compress + D2H on an internal CUDA stream and ``wait_compress_async``\nsynchronises it.  It serves the ``gpu_direct`` KV producer mode (the default\nfor ``--kv-comp p4flat``).  The ``cpu_after_raw_swap`` producer is served by\nthe :class:`P4FlatCPUKVCompressor` subclass below (CPU worker-pool encode);\nboth share the same GPU decode kernel and on-host storage layout.\n\nIt subclasses :class:`DietGPUKVCompressor` purely to reuse the codec-agnostic\npersistent-slot bookkeeping (``_assign_kv_slot`` / ``_free_kv_slot`` /\n``has_*`` / ``free_persistent_block`` / ``decompress_batch`` chunking).  The\nstorage layout and the codec are completely different and overridden below.\n\nStorage layout (per layer, per K and V), one dense pool of variable-length\ncompressed blobs indexed by physical slot:\n  - ``blob``       : pinned [host_n, max_comp_size] uint8.  Each row holds a\n    serialised compressed block ``[headers | codes | sm | codec |\n    exc_idx | exc_val]`` (or, on raw fallback, the raw BF16 bytes).\n  - ``total_size`` : pinned [host_n] int32 — used bytes of the blob row.\n  - ``exc_cnt``    : pinned [host_n] int32 — number of exceptions.\n  - ``is_raw``     : pinned [host_n] uint8 — 0 compressed, 1 raw BF16 stored\n    in-row, 2 raw BF16 retained only in secondary KV (tight-stride overflow).\n\nA KV block of shape ``block_shape`` is flattened to ``block_numel`` BF16\nelements and reshaped to a 2-D ``[M_b, K_b]`` matrix with both dims multiples\nof 64 (p4flat requires this).  The reshape is a contiguous view, so the codec\nstays bit-exact; the (M_b, K_b) factoring only affects the compression ratio.\n``block_numel`` must therefore be a multiple of 64*64 = 4096.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport ctypes\nimport ctypes\nimport glob\nimport heapq\nimport logging\nimport os\n            \"cores 0-%d reserved for forward\",\n            idx, affinity[0], affinity[-1], len(affinity), nt,\n            self._reserve_cores - 1)\n\n    def _probe_sizes(self, M_b: int, K_b: int) -> Tuple[int, int, int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Analytic sizes — no GPU.  The CPU encoder stores sm row-major\n        (``row_major_sm=1``) and ``subtile_codec`` all-``0xFF``.\"\"\"\n        num_tiles = (M_b // 64) * (K_b // 64)\n        hb = num_tiles * 16\n        cb = M_b * K_b // 2\n        smb = M_b * K_b\n        cdb = (M_b // 16) * (K_b // 16)\n        self._idx_dtype = torch.int32\n        self._val_dtype = torch.int16\n        self._idx_es = 4\n        self._val_es = 2\n        self._row_major_sm = 1\n        return hb, cb, smb, cdb\n\n    # gpu_direct path is not supported on this subclass — it is the\n    # cpu_after_raw_swap encoder.  For GPU-side p4flat compression use the\n    # base P4FlatKVCompressor (selected by TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_PRODUCER=\n    # gpu_direct, which is the default for --kv-comp p4flat).\n    def compress_batch_async(self, layer_id, block_ids, gpu_k, gpu_v):\n        raise NotImplementedError(\n            \"P4FlatCPUKVCompressor is the CPU-encode (cpu_after_raw_swap) \"\n            \"backend; it does not support the gpu_direct producer.  For GPU \"\n            \"compression use TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_PRODUCER=gpu_direct (the \"\n            \"default for --kv-comp p4flat), which selects P4FlatKVCompressor.\")\n\n    def _release_quarantined_slot(self, layer_id: int, slot: int) -> None:\n        free_set = self._kv_free_slots[layer_id]\n        hwm = self._kv_active_count[layer_id]\n        if slot == hwm - 1:\n            hwm -= 1\n            while hwm - 1 in free_set:\n                free_set.discard(hwm - 1)\n                hwm -= 1\n            self._kv_active_count[layer_id] = hwm\n        else:\n            free_set.add(slot)\n                    offload_backend, role=\"offload\")\n            # Legacy alias.  Most call sites that used self.weight_compressor\n            # directly were dealing with offload/frozen_compressed paths; we\n            # alias to the offload compressor so they keep behaving the\n            # same when the user supplies only the base flag.\n            self.weight_compressor = self._compressor_offload\n\n        env_var_value = os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_USE_KV_COMP\")\n        use_kv_comp = env_var_value is not None and env_var_value == \"1\"\n        DualMemoryLoader.no_offload_kv = (\n            os.getenv(\"TIERED_SERVE_NO_OFFLOAD_KV\", \"0\") == \"1\")\n        if DualMemoryLoader.no_offload_kv:\n            # KV stays fully resident in GPU HBM: disable offload + KV\n            # compression entirely (weights are still offloaded).\n            use_kv_comp = False\n        DualMemoryLoader.use_kv_comp = use_kv_comp\n        DualMemoryLoader.kv_full_block_only = False\n\n        self.kv_compressor = None\n        if DualMemoryLoader.use_kv_comp:\n            kv_comp_backend = os.getenv(\n                \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_BACKEND\", \"zipserv\").lower()\n            if kv_comp_backend not in (\n                    \"zipserv\", \"dietgpu\", \"mantexp\", \"p4flat\", \"p4flatcpu\",\n                    \"bitcomp\", \"bitcompcpu\", \"ublb_flat\", \"ublb_tbe\",\n                    \"chunk_delta3\"):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"Unknown TIERED_SERVE_KV_COMP_BACKEND: \"\n                    f\"{kv_comp_backend!r}. Expected one of: \"\n                    f\"zipserv, dietgpu, mantexp, p4flat, p4flatcpu, \"\n                    f\"bitcomp, bitcompcpu, ublb_flat, ublb_tbe, \"\n                    f\"chunk_delta3.\")\n\n            _full_block_only = (\n                os.getenv(\n                    \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_FULL_BLOCK_ONLY\", \"0\") == \"1\")\n            from tiered_serve.kv_codec_spec import supports_full_block_only\n            if (_full_block_only\n                    and not supports_full_block_only(kv_comp_backend)):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_FULL_BLOCK_ONLY=1 currently requires \"\n                    \"the p4flat, p4flatcpu, or chunk_delta3 KV backend; got \"\n                    f\"{kv_comp_backend!r}\")\n            DualMemoryLoader.kv_full_block_only = _full_block_only\n\n            # ── KV compression producer mode ──\n            # Selects how the compressed KV copy is produced during unload.\n            # Both modes always store raw KV in LPDDR secondary so that\n            # prefill-containing phases load uncompressed without paying\n            # decompression latency.  Resolved *before* the backend is\n            # instantiated because p4flat picks its encode implementation\n            # (GPU vs CPU) from the producer mode below.\n            #\n            #   gpu_direct:\n            #       Backend's existing pipeline produces compressed KV on GPU\n            #       (DietGPU/MantExp/p4flat run compress kernels on\n            #       comp_stream).  Raw secondary unload runs in parallel.\n            #\n            #   cpu_after_raw_swap:\n            #       Avoid GPU compression entirely.  Raw KV is D2H'd to\n            #       LPDDR secondary first, then a CPU compressor reads\n            #       directly from secondary_kv (no extra D2H) and writes\n            #       into the persistent compressed host pool.  Supported only\n            #       by backends that ship a CPU encoder: ZipServ (C++ worker\n            #       manager), p4flat, and ChunkDelta3 (Python worker boundary\n            #       around an OpenMP C++ encoder).\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run the canonical 70B offline performance matrix in isolated processes.\n\nset -Eeuo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../..\" && pwd)\"\n\nMODEL=\"meta-llama/Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct\"\nINPUT_SEQ_LEN=1020\nGEN_TOKENS=129\nWARMUP=16\nPREFILL_CHUNK=8192\nREPEATS=3\nKV_BACKEND=\"p4flat\"\nGPU_INDEX=0\nNUMA_NODE=0\nWEIGHT_HUGE_PAGES=14\nMAX_IDLE_HBM_MIB=1024\nCLEANUP_TIMEOUT=120\nOUTPUT_ROOT=\"${REPO_ROOT}/benchmark_results/offline_suite\"\nDRY_RUN=0\nCHECK_ONLY=0\nBREAKDOWN=0\nSTART_FROM=\"\"\nBATCHES=(1 16 32 64 96 128)\n\nPYTHON=\"${REPO_ROOT}/.venv/bin/python\"\nDRIVER=\"${REPO_ROOT}/offline_offload_kvweight.py\"\nSTACK_POOL=\"${REPO_ROOT}/etc/stack_pool.so\"\nHUGEPAGE_SYSFS=\"/sys/kernel/mm/hugepages/hugepages-16777216kB\"\n\nMETHODS=(\n  flexgen\n  flexgen-zipserv\n  flexgen-zipserv-fused\n  cao-zipserv\n  cao-zipserv-fused\n  cao-zipserv-fused-kvcomp\n  cao-p4flat-fused\n  cao-p4flat-fused-kvcomp\n  cao-cd3\n  cao-cd3-fused\n  cao-cd3-fused-kvcomp\n)\n\nusage() {\n  cat <<'EOF'\nUsage: bash scripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh [OPTIONS]\n\nRuns the configured offline performance matrix. Every configuration and\nrepeat starts a fresh Python process. The next run starts only after the GPU,\n16 GiB HugePages, and tiered-serve processes return to an idle state.\n\nOptions:\n  --methods LIST          Comma/space-separated method IDs (default: all)\n  --batches LIST          Comma/space-separated batches (default: 1,16,32,64,96,128)\n  --repeats N             Fresh-process repeats per method (default: 3)\n  --input-seq-len N       Random input tokens per request (default: 1020)\n  --gen N                 Tokens 